    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneIV_13.8/p@169659",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "CADE.\nWas ever feather so lightly blown to and fro as this multitude? The name of Henry the Fifth hales them to an hundred mischiefs and makes them leave me desolate. I see them lay their heads together to surprise me. My sword make way for me, for here is no staying.—In despite of the devils and hell, have through the very middest of you! And heavens and honour be witness that no want of resolution in me, but only my followers’ base and ignominious treasons, makes me betake me to my heels.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneIV_13.8/p@169659/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 5,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneIV_13.8/p@169659/line-2",
          "start": 6,
          "end": 495,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
